# Archived builds are byte-exact by contract: archive-testdata.js verifies
# each file byte-for-byte against the committed blob it came from, so no
# checkout may ever smudge them to CRLF. -text disables all line-ending
# conversion in BOTH directions for this directory, on every machine,
# regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to testdata/ as a whole: the current test files
# are written CRLF by export_to_platform.py on Windows and normalized to LF
# blobs by autocrlf at commit — pinning them -text would flip future commits
# to CRLF blobs and bury real content changes under whole-file EOL diffs.
# Nothing byte-compares the current files against blobs (the archiver reads
# them only for their testVersion string), so autocrlf's behavior is right
# for them and load-bearing for the archive's.
testdata/archive/** -text
